From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: mux UART2 on the EVB 26-pin header

The EVB header exposes UART2 on XGPIOB[11] TX and XGPIOB[12] RX. UART1
shares its RX pad with the onboard blue LED (XGPIOA[29]), so on this
carrier UART2 is the usable SLIP/HaLow port.

The bootloader leaves these pads at their default function: the UART2
controller probes, but nothing reaches the header. Raw fmux 0 selects
UART2 on these pads (fmux 5 would route them to UART4), per the vendor
cv181x pinmux table. The pads live in the RTC IO domain, which the EVB
runs at 3.3 V like the header pins.

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-duomodule01-evb.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-duomodule01-evb.dts
@@ -146,6 +146,15 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	uart2_cfg: uart2-cfg {
+		uart2-pins {
+			pinmux = <PINMUX(PIN_UART2_TX, 0)>,
+				 <PINMUX(PIN_UART2_RX, 0)>;
+			drive-strength-microamp = <10800>;
+			power-source = <3300>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	sdhci1_cfg: sdhci1-cfg {
 		/* Vendor U-Boot cvi_sdio1_pad_setting: CLK pull-down, CMD/DAT
 		 * pull-up, drive strength left at the weakest default. */
@@ -316,6 +325,8 @@
  * and the UART card in Settings shows it. UART1 is muxed by S31slip; the
  * other pads need a board-specific fmux setup before use. */
 &uart2 {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&uart2_cfg>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
